<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tallapoosa River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tallapoosa is a river of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alabama">Alabama</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, which joins the Coosa to form the Alabama River. Many of the Upper Towns of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Muscogee</a> stood on its banks, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrew-jackson">Andrew Jackson</a>'s defeat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sticks">Red Sticks</a> at Horseshoe Bend in 1814 took place in one of its bends.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tallapoosa-river.jpg" alt="Tallapoosa River" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Elvissa · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_Tallapoosa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
